A||N||16||Fiero5||What is your favorite Star Trek?||||6||
Z||000000||Fiero5||11-12-2001||08:03 PM||||1) What is your favorite Star Trek series?<BR>A; TOS<BR>B: TNG<BR>C: DS9<BR>D: VOY<BR>E: ENT<P>2) What are some of your favorite Star Trek episodes from each of them?<P>3) What are your favorite Star Trek characters from each?<P>4) What is your favorite Star Trek movie?<P>5) Did you as a kid or do you now collect Star Trek memorabilia?<P>Here are mine:<BR>1) A: TOS<P>2) I have a lot, but I guess  <BR>A: "Arena", "Elaan of Troyus", I'll think of others<BR>B: "Yesterdays Enterprise", "Best of Both Worlds", <BR>C: "Trials and Tribbleations"<BR>D: Can't think of one of the episode names at the moment-will come back and edit later<BR>E: The Andorian one was pretty good<P>3) My favorite characters are:<BR>A: Kirk, Spock, Sulu, Gorn and Baloks puppet<BR>B: Picard, Data & Darmok<BR>C: Never did get into DS9 much, but I guess Worf in later episodes<BR>D: Janeway & Seven of Nine<BR>E: Too early for me yet<P>4) My Favorite Star Trek movie would have to be "First Contact".<P>5) I have very fond memories of collecting Star Trek when I was a kid. I remember early on seeing the AMT model "The Exploration set" in a T.V. Guide and my Dad sending away for it. It seemed to take forever to get it, and then before the model glue was even dry I rushed outside to play with them. We used to go to Kennebunkport Maine every year for Vacation. The best part for me wasn't going to the beach during the day, but going up to the Portland mall that evening. Stores like Spencer Gifts way back then was Star Trek heaven!<P>Oh well, let's hear from some others..<P>Steve<BR><P>------------------<BR>                                     <IMG SRC="http://images.animfactory.com/animations/holiday_events/thanksgiving/turkey_season_md_wht.gif">  <BR>                                <BR>http://kelleyfamilyfieros.50megs.com||||reg||6
Z||000001||Formula88||11-13-2001||09:30 AM||||Well, they each have their advantages.  I think the writing in TOS was the best, followed by some of TNG.  TNG really got boring fast after 4th season.  I never really cared for DS9, but if I'd gotten interested when the Dominion War started, it might have kept my interest.  And, of course, Battlestar Voyager wasn't too bad either.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>My favorite episodes:<BR>TOS: The Enterprise Incident<BR>TOS: Balance of Terror<BR>TOS: Mirror, Mirror<BR>TOS: Doomsday Machine<P>TNG: Best of Both Worlds<BR>TNG: Yesterday's Enterprise<BR>TNG: The Measure of a Man<BR>TNG: D'ar Mok<P>DS9: Any episode with Kira's evil double in that tight black leather bodysuit.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>VOY: feh - no real favorites, but Seven is nice eye candy.<P>ENT: too early to say.  I like the concept of the show.  So far it seems to be pretty good.  I like the sets and the look.  It's okay that they're a bit more Kirkish and brash, but they've got to be careful not to make them swaggering cowboys.  Our Astronauts today aren't THAT bad.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Oh, and Jolene Blalock gets my vote for most attractive Star Trek babe to date.  Wow!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pheagey||11-13-2001||09:41 AM||||So many choices!!!aaaaa<BR>   I dunno they each have good points and bad. Ent. looks to be the best all around (visuals etc.) but TOS was good because w/o where woul dwe be?...TNG we good 'cause it carrid on the liniage but didn't quick have a lot of physical elements (ala Kirk fist fights). so many.......<BR>"..second star to the right and striahgt on till morning..."<P>------------------<BR>'88 coupe, 5 speed.<BR>"The car formerly know as Dj's Fiero."||||reg||1
Z||000003||87ECOsomething||11-13-2001||10:12 AM||||I'm not a huge Star Trek fan but I did kinda get into TNG.<P>Two of my favorite TNG episodes:<P>'Cause and Effect' - Enterprise caught in a temporal loop and blew up several times before the crew figured out they were reliving the same moment in time over and over again.<P>can't remember title - It was the cliffhanger where the crew went back in time to 1800's San Francisco and found Data'a head in an old mine shaft (also had an appearance by Mark Twain).||||reg||14
Z||000004||Butter||11-13-2001||04:38 PM||||The first one with Captain Pike.  That episode seems to have started something.||||reg||1
Z||000005||SwissFormula||11-13-2001||06:39 PM||||My favorite character is Seven, Spock on second place.<P>Live long and prosper...<P>Roy<P>------------------<BR>88 Formula, T-Top<BR>1 of 20 Fieros in Switzerland||||reg||6
Z||000006||DJRice||11-13-2001||07:26 PM||||I liked "First Contact" and "The Wrath of Kahn" the best as far as the movies go.<P>As far as the series go, I dont really have too many favorite episodes of any of the series, but I do enjoy watching TOS.  I liked most of TNG with the exception of Wesley Crusher Boy Wonder.  I thought that Voyager got right back to what Star Trek was all about and enjoyed those episodes immensely.  Enterprise looks to be quite promising.  <P>I have a small collection of Star Trek Micromachines and some of the figurines from First Contact and The Next Generation.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djr_signature.jpg"> <BR>"And this one time, on the Fiero Forum..."||||reg||1
Z||000007||DaRkLoRD||11-13-2001||10:04 PM||||87EC: Time's Arrow.. awesome episodes.. a bit of trivia, the actor that played Twain was the same guy that was Deep Throat on X-Files.. (Jerry Hardin I believe..)<P>Hmm.. TNG was good, I loved the last few seasons of DS9.. Voyager was ok, but I never really got into it.. As for Enterprise.. it has potential.. but so far has been a major Voyager re-hash (except for the Andorian episode, that was pretty TOS-ish..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<P>Fav episodes..<P>TOS:<BR>hmm.. can't think of any off the top of my head, though I really liked some of the movies!<P>TNG:<BR>Times Arrow<BR>Best of Both Worlds<BR>Yesterday's Enterprise<P>DS9:<BR>Trials & Tribblations<BR>Almost any one in the last couple of seasons<BR>Any one with Ezri Dax... MMMM...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Voyager:<BR>The one where they went to 1996...<P>Enterprise:<BR>Too early to tell..<P>Fav Characaters:<P>TOS: all of em!<P>TNG:<BR>Picard<BR>Data<BR>Ensign Robyn Lefler!! (mmm.. ashley judd...)<P>DS9:<BR>Sisko kicks ass...<BR>Ezri... d@mn she's cute.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Enterprise:<BR>so far they're all pretty cool!<BR>Ensign Sato's pretty cute, with T'Pol being a very close second.<P>Fav trek movie.. Generations.. ST6 was really good too.<P>nope, no ST stuff.. I have a bunch of the books though.<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000008||My7Fieros||11-14-2001||01:47 AM||||Hmmmmm....lets see.....<BR>TNG fav eps:<BR>Yesterday's Enterprise (with the Enterprise C)<P>The one where Scotty was on it and was bugging everybody and made the original Enterprise bridge on the hollodeck<P>TOS fav eps:<BR>Doomsday machine<P>The one where that giant hand is holding the Enterprise by the saucer section<P>Voyager fav eps:<BR>Ehhh....they were all ok, so so.....<P>DS9 fav eps:<BR>Didnt like DS9<P>Enterprise fav eps:<BR>Ive liked all so far (all that Ive seen rather)<P>Fav movies:<BR>ST2,4 (Im looking for thih nuclear wessels  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ), Generations, and First Contact.<P>TNG were my favs.....I like Picard, hes kinda got that Sean Connery accent..."The line will be drawn he-uh! Thish nonsensh mush shtop!"   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Troy is a hottie...much better now than in the 80s w/that rediculas hair!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 11-14-2001).]||||reg||1
