Z||000014||Cliff Pennock||11-16-2001||07:32 PM||||I just watched the first three episodes of Enterprise (it isn't on tv yet so I had to download them) adn I must say I like it a lot already!<P>TOS: That was great when I was a kid, but if I watch it now, it's just a bit to... 70-ish. My favorite character is Dr. McCoy ("He's dead, Jim").<P>TNG: Awesome! Seen all episodes at least twice! Picard is the perfect captain for the Federation's flagship. And Patrick Stewart is a very good actor. Favorite characters: Picard, Q ("Jean Luck Pickerd? Package for Jean Luck Pickerd?"), Data, Dr. Crusher (did she get more beautiful when she got older?) and Riker.<P>DS9: Okay I guess, I just don't like the fact they made Sisko the most important man of the Federation all of a sudden. I loved the episode where Q kept comparing him with Picard and how much more he liked Picard. Favorite characters: Kira, Jadzia, Quark. Thouroughly dislike Sisko.<P>VOY: Can anyone explain to me what they were thinking when they casted Kate Mulgrew as Janeway? I never liked Voyager because there were too many things they did "wrong". Voyager is in the same time as TNG, and in TNG they made it clear the Federation had no "warships" (just science vessels armed to the teeth  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ). Voyager was introduced as a warship. Also, no Federation ship was able to land itself on planets because there was absoluty no need for it. Voyager landed on the surface of a planet in one of the first episodes. And I just hate the casting. Favorite characters: if I had to choose one, it would be the doctor.<P>ENT: Cool! Much better than I thought it would be! I love the way they introduce stuff that has become "normal" in the other series ("It's called a phase-pistol, it has two settings: 'Kill' and 'Stun'", "They've locked on to us with some kind of stabilizing beam!"). Favorite chars so far: Archer and of course T'Pol.<P>I used to have all these die-cast Star Trek models of all Enterprises (except of course NX-01), and a few other ships. Some of them I had worked on for months. I was especially proud of the NCC-1701D I had built because it had over 400 lights! It looked beautiful! But I also have two cats, and they seemed to like them a bit less. None of the models survived...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||DaRkLoRD||11-16-2001||10:06 PM||||I'm starting to like Enterprise more and more. they finally have GOOD uniforms.. not like the pajamas that all the other series wore!<P>it's cool that they haven't got shields etc yet.. well, interesting at least. though the holodeck thing in an early episode was lame.. that's supposed to be "new" tech in TNG, and yet the Klingons have it, 200 years before that? yeah right.<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
